      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-305231",
      ":question/problem": "An office supplier is loading boxes of paper and toner cartridges onto a dolly. The dolly can carry no more than $160$ pounds. Each box of paper weighs $9.5$ pounds, and each box of toner weighs $11.2$ pounds. The number of toner boxes must be no more than the number of paper boxes. Let $p$ represent the number of paper boxes and $t$ represent the number of toner boxes, where $p$ and $t$ are nonnegative integers. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The system of inequalities that models this situation is the following:\n$9.5p + 11.2t \\ge 160$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}"
